  "reference_protocol": "Both drivers receive complete SQL statements on separate input lines. Compare output, return codes, normalized diagnostics, stored catalog/rows/rowids and reference integrity results. Two tests use controlled pre-existing invalid CHECK/type data; the writable-schema fixture explicitly disables the reference shell defensive option during temporary fixture creation only. Neither production driver nor result comparison disables or filters checks.",
  "architecture": "An explicit CREATE STRICT AST variant is independently replayed. Strict type names and implicit non-rowid primary NOT NULL rules are validated before ordinary Core construction. ANY lowers to a no-affinity physical Core column, while the retained catalog type program preserves the public ANY name. Expressions, comparisons and default storage therefore use BLOB/no affinity; metadata uses the original declared type. Cached strict type programs are checked against stored candidate values through the existing row-constraint boundary before CHECK evaluation, and datatype failures remain Except errors under OR IGNORE/REPLACE.",
  "alter_scope": "The pinned SQLite implementation scans existing STRICT rows after every ADD, including old CHECK clauses. The port validates new declared types, lowers ANY, scans types and checks in row order and reports type mismatch on DEFAULT before publication.",
  "schema_iteration": "sqlite_sequence enters the live hash before its first AUTOINCREMENT owner, while its sqlite_schema row follows the owner. The connection now tracks those two orders separately; existing bucket growth, reload and transaction/savepoint behavior remains in the pinned hash model.",
  "proof_scope": "Audited component contracts cover ANY acceptance/lowering and successful type validation. Compiled type-program equality and a source-aware STRICT construction trace connect retention to the lowered schema. Existing Core row/index/storage invariants and the twelve-host-binding boundary remain. These contracts do not prove full SQLite type semantics, integrity-check diagnostics, whole-SQL equivalence or every physical failure schedule.",
  "feature_probe_scope": "The 88-case unittest and separate fresh-seed survey use the same named feature families/generator. Their 20-to-18 failure change closes the STRICT probe only; it is not an independent-generator result or a global compatibility percentage.",
