  "limitations": [
    "STRICT support is limited to the admitted persistent rowid-table/ordinary-column subset. Generated columns, WITHOUT ROWID, TEMP/attached schemas and the existing type/index/constraint admission limits are not established by this checkpoint.",
    "table_list lists modeled tables and built-in main/temp catalogs in the pinned 64-bit schema order. Views, virtual/shadow tables, attached/temp user objects and virtual-table metadata introspection remain limited.",
    "Runtime quick_check/integrity_check support and malformed-file behavior are not made complete here; comparison snapshots use reference SQLite to inspect both resulting files. The controlled invalid-type example exercises one admissible physical-value shape, not every corrupt STRICT image.",
    "Composite references/primary keys, deferred/other FK actions, declared non-BINARY collations, views/triggers, UTF-16 and expression/partial indexes remain among the wider SQL/storage limitations.",
    "The 60 SIGKILL samples cover established storage paths rather than all STRICT, type-error or schema-invalidation schedules."
  ],
